WEBVTT

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:00.820
Alfredo Sotto Corpuz: Observers are commanded to keep silent under pain

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:07.440
Alfredo Sotto Corpuz: of penalty while the impeachment court is in session for the trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:12.370
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The impeachment trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:14.010
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: is hereby called to order.

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:18.790
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: We shall be led in prayer by Senator Judge Bam Aquino.

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:58.030
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Here is a prayer written by Pope St. Leo the Great whose feast day we celebrate today. Let us pray. Hear, O Lord. Hear our prayer, O Lord. And grant us a heart to love you and an earnest desire to please you in all things. Give us, O Lord, the light of your Spirit that we may see the way in which we should walk. Grant that we may not turn aside to the right hand or to the left, but may follow the path of your commandments with an upright heart. May your love be the guide of our actions and your grace our support in every trial, so that we may grow daily in holiness and reach the fullness of eternal life. Amen.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:03.390
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Amen. The clerk of court will now call the roll.

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:51.440
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Roll call of members. Senator Judge Aquino. Senator Judge Cayetano Alan. Senator Judge Cayetano Pia. Senator Judge De La Rosa. Senator Judge Ejercito. Senator Judge Estrada. Senator Judge Go. Senator Judge Hontiveros. Senator Judge Lacson. Senator Judge Lapid. Senator Judge Legarda. Senator Judge Marcoleta. Senator Judge Marcos. Senator Judge Padilla, Senator Judge Pangilinan, Senator Judge Sotto III, Senator Judge Tulfo Erwin, Senator Judge Tulfo Raffy, Senator Judge Villanueva, Senator Judge Villar Camille, Senator Judge Villar Mark, Senator Judge Zubiri, The Presiding Officer, Senator Judge Escudero, The Senate President, Senator Judge Gatchalian.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:55.500
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: With 12 Senator Judges present, we declare the presence of a quorum.

00:09:57.650 --> 00:10:05.890
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: In accordance with the rules of procedure on impeachment trials, the chair now recognizes the duly elected presiding officer to preside over the proceedings of the impeachment court.

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:07.290
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Mr. Senate President.

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:21.810
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: With the permission of the body, before I recognize Senator Judge Sotto, if there are no objections, we shall dispense with the reading of the November 9, 2026 Journal of the Senate sitting as an impeachment court and shall consider the same as approved.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:25.040
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Sotto, what

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:25.820
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: is your pleasure, sir?

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:54.680
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Good morning. Mr. Presiding Officer. Just as a reminder and perhaps to refresh my memory, is it not we have penalties and sanctions against those who lie before the impeachment court? Will you please refresh my memory on this matter so that the witnesses and the prosecution and the defense will be reminded as well?

00:10:55.950 --> 00:11:26.060
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: They may be subject to contempt by the court, Mr. Your Honor. And in addition to that, may be subjected to cases of perjury should one be filed against him before the proper prosecutor's office and or courts of law. Because the statements given by any witness is under oath and is therefore covered by our laws on perjury as well. What is the pleasure of Senator Judge Lacson?

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:26.580
Sen. Panfilo “Ping” M. Lacson: Thank you, sir.

00:11:29.050 --> 00:12:39.830
Sen. Panfilo “Ping” M. Lacson: Just to supplement, sir, I was about to make the same manifestation, but since the former Senate President already made the same manifestation, I would just like to supplement by way of mentioning Rule 5 under Resolution 39. This was adopted by the Senate Impeachment Court in March of 2011. And it expressly grants the impeachment court the power to cite for contempt of the court anybody for that matter. And yesterday was not a good day for the impeachment court, Mr. President, Mr. Presiding Officer, simply because we had a witness who smirked, who laughed, almost made a mockery of the impeachment trial. And we don't want to have a repeat of that kind of testimony. So, just a reminder to everyone that this is not an implied power of the impeachment court, Mr. Presiding Officer, but an express power granted by such resolution. Thank you.

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:47.750
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Duly noted and well taken. Thank you, Senator Judge Lacson. What is the pleasure of the Senate President?

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:53.570
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Just to correct the number of senators earlier, we have 13 senator judges present.

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:59.970
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Before calling on the next witness, Chair would like to state something also in relation to

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:02.090
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Engineer Jimmy yesterday.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:15.330
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yesterday, a request was made by Senator Judge Aquino as well as Senator Judge Hontiveros for the list of properties.

00:13:16.860 --> 00:14:09.020
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: owned and or in the name of singularly or jointly of Attorney Carpio and the Vice President. For the record, for the information of the Senator Judges, we have not received such a report from Engineer Adalin. Neither have we received a copy or name of the travel agency requested by Senator Judge Rafi Tulfo. The Chair therefore directs the Clerk of Court to kindly communicate with Engineer Adalin and follow up on the same. If by tomorrow the same is not yet complied with, unless sufficient cause or reason is given, the Court will be forced to issue compulsory process on the same. Yes, what is the pleasure of Senator Judge Risa?

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:36.830
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat tabi, Mr. Presiding Officer. Unless the Presiding Officer will indeed give Engineer Adalin until tomorrow to submit the court's requested documents, may I just remind all of us that I actually requested him and he committed to furnishing us those documents within yesterday, Mr. Presiding Officer. Salamat.

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:53.710
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Again, chair reiterates his directive to the clerk of court to kindly communicate with him and to kindly explain, to kindly comply and or explain why he has not yet been able to comply and if at all when he can comply.

