Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Yes, Your Honor. But if you could just specify that we are willing to stipulate again with respect to purpose number one regarding his... position as the City Assessor of City Garden of Samal. And again, similar to yesterday, we take strong exception to the allegations that the position of the respondent or of the prosecution was falsely and maliciously done. That the property reflected in that TSN was not reflected in the SALN. Considering that same As the property discussed yesterday in Matina, Davao, in this property also, there are glaring discrepancies between that property contained in the TSN and the property contained in the TSN, which would show that they're completely different properties and there's no way that this witness could prove that they're the same properties. All that he could testify to is again, at most, they're in the same barangay.

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:33.090
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Your Honor, can we just move to strike the manifestation of the counsel for the prosecution? It appears that he is testifying, Your Honor.

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:45.190
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Definitely not. And the terms malicious and falsely made came from the defense. So they cannot expect us to take that sitting down and not vehemently object to it.

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:47.710
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: It is part of our offer of testimony.

00:20:47.710 --> 00:20:50.830
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Which is improper. That's why I'm responding to it accordingly.

00:20:51.190 --> 00:21:02.670
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: It is not improper because we want this honorable court to appreciate the testimony of this witness in that light, Your Honor. And we're stating the fact.

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.300
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: We will just leave the matter to the judicious discretion.

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:05.880
