01:39:54.650 --> 01:39:55.550
Engr. John Kenneth D. Enumerables: Yes, Your Honor.

01:39:55.690 --> 01:39:56.690
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Dito sa Kembali Coast?

01:39:56.970 --> 01:39:57.570
Engr. John Kenneth D. Enumerables: Yes, Your Honor.

01:39:57.750 --> 01:39:59.070
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Maraming salamat, Engineer.

01:39:59.490 --> 01:40:03.800
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you. Senator Judge Villanueva, you may proceed, sir. You have two minutes.

01:40:08.560 --> 01:40:10.100
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

01:40:11.800 --> 01:40:26.470
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Ganda nga po, no? Akta ng dahali. Sir, una, nung tinatanong po kayo about Barangay Matanos, sabi niyo walang Barangay Matanos, pero ngayon sinasabi niyo halos lahat ng titulo nakalagay Matanos.

01:40:27.100 --> 01:40:28.640
Engr. John Kenneth D. Enumerables: Doon po sa titulo yun.

01:40:30.630 --> 01:40:41.770
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Pero bakit po kanina ang tagal niyong malaman na may barangay matanos? Kasi nalito po kami. So yung San Isidro, barangay San Isidro, wala po yan sa mga titulo?

01:40:42.470 --> 01:40:50.110
Engr. John Kenneth D. Enumerables: Sa titulo po ng Kimbali po, hindi po nakalagay yung San Isidro. Lahat po matanos po nakalagay.

01:40:53.410 --> 01:41:26.700
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Ngayon, doon po sa dalawang, masasabi po ba agad natin na iisang lupa talaga? Yung binabanggit dito sa usapin natin dito sa Korte dahil lang doon sa description na binabanggit nyo o meron po bang ibang detalya pa na kailangan po nating paghambingin para masiguro talaga natin na itong dalawang dokumento ay tumutukoy sa isang parcel of land. Yung pong itong TCT No. 142-2019-013134.

01:41:32.360 --> 01:41:48.920
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Uulitin ko yung tanong ko po. Meron po ba tayong iba pang detalye na kailangang makita, malaman, para masiguro natin, mapaghambing natin, na matiyak natin na ito pong dalawang dokumento ay tumutukoy sa iisang parcel of land?

01:41:49.930 --> 01:41:56.760
Engr. John Kenneth D. Enumerables: Sa opisina po ng City Assurance Office po, mayroon kaming dokumento yung total landholding po.

01:41:57.080 --> 01:41:57.680
Sen. Joel Villanueva: I'm sorry,

01:41:57.680 --> 01:41:58.280
Sen. Joel Villanueva: sorry, total?

01:41:58.580 --> 01:42:07.620
Engr. John Kenneth D. Enumerables: Total landholding po. So makita po doon kung ilang property po ang naka-declare ng isang tao po.

01:42:08.100 --> 01:42:54.970
Sen. Joel Villanueva: O kasi nga po ito po, yung March 15, 2018, deed of absolute sale, in-identify po yung pag-purchase nitong property. Pero doon sa reported 2019, SALN, nakalagay acquisition year of 2013. Pag tinignan niyo po ito, may limang taong gap. Limang taon yung acquisition gap. Kung talaga pong nakuha na yung property noong 2013, meron ho ba kayo sa inyong opisina na magpapatunay na dokumento na ito ay nakuha noong 2013 at the same po yung property na yon dito sa 2018 deed of absolute sale?

01:42:56.480 --> 01:42:59.060
Engr. John Kenneth D. Enumerables: Will we reply po sa opisina po kung meron po?

01:42:59.570 --> 01:43:01.010
Sen. Joel Villanueva: O hindi niyo po sigurado?

01:43:02.530 --> 01:43:06.990
Engr. John Kenneth D. Enumerables: Ah, kasi po wala akong dalawang dokumento. We will verify.

01:43:07.390 --> 01:43:08.150
Sen. Joel Villanueva: So

01:43:08.150 --> 01:43:43.150
Sen. Joel Villanueva: kung iaharap po sa inyo yung tax declaration at ang SALN entry na nagsasabi po na may residential property dito sa Matanos o Kaputian District, maaari po ba ninyong matukoy kung ang dalawang dokumento ay tumutukoy sa iisang lupa? Sa inyong professional na karanasan, experience o kaalaman at batay po doon sa official records ng inyong tanggapan, ano po yung masasabi nyo tungkol doon sa pagkakatugma ng property na binabanggit po natin? Exactly the same po ba?

01:43:43.370 --> 01:43:45.110
Engr. John Kenneth D. Enumerables: Yes, Your Honor. Isa lang po yun.

01:43:45.750 --> 01:43:47.890
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Salamat po, Mr. Witness. Thank you.

01:43:50.180 --> 01:45:09.660
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Villanueva. Chair confirms. The statement earlier made by Attorney Linden pertaining to the testimony of Mr. Marco Pineda, the Acting Register of Deeds of IGACOS, on October 1, specifically for the information of Senator Judges, pages 95 to 97, upon the inquiry made by the presiding officer, where Mr. Pineda confirmed that Nanggaling daw kasi sa mother title yung mga nakalagay sa titulo at nakalagay sa mother title Matanos pa rin at under PD 1529. Hindi po daw nila pwedeng baguhin yun at kine-carry over lang nila gamit niyang salita mula sa ina papunta sa anak nung titulo at kaya na-carry over po yung titulong yun at para malaman daw para sigurado na yun yung parehong lupa. Ay kailangan tingnan sa tax mapping sa City Assessor's Office para matingnan at makita kung yun nga po ay pareho o magkaibang piraso ng lupa yun. Chair would like to make some interjections. Atty. Tolosa, you made mention of the fact na unang dineklara yung lupa, 2013?

01:45:11.180 --> 01:45:23.220
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Yes, Your Honor. And actually not 2013 because I think the Vice President was not in public office at that time. So I think it was declared first in 2015.

01:45:23.840 --> 01:45:24.280
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Sorry, it was

01:45:24.280 --> 01:45:28.360
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: declared in 2015 but made mention of the sale

01:45:28.360 --> 01:45:29.120
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: in 2013.

01:45:29.460 --> 01:45:30.320
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Yes, yes, your honor.

01:45:30.460 --> 01:45:31.380
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: And they placed installment.

01:45:31.980 --> 01:45:35.060
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Yes, that is the mode of payment, installment.

01:45:35.180 --> 01:45:35.700
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Under

01:45:35.700 --> 01:45:38.540
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: the deed of sale, ilan taon po yung installment?

01:45:41.270 --> 01:45:46.310
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: I think the schedule of payments was not indicated in the deed

01:45:46.310 --> 01:45:46.530
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: of sale.

01:45:46.670 --> 01:45:55.970
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So natanggal yung installment. Diba? At the particular year, if I recall correctly, after five years in 2018, na wala na yung installment, nilagay na niya na sale.

01:45:57.730 --> 01:46:02.230
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So I presume na natapos na installment on the fifth year.

01:46:02.810 --> 01:46:17.940
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: But you're on that point. That's why we asked the witness to confirm a while ago that there is no contract to sell annotated in the transfer certificate of titles or mentioned in the deed of absolute sale.

01:46:19.520 --> 01:46:26.280
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: If the only document that we have here is the deed of absolute sale which was executed in 2018.

01:46:26.620 --> 01:47:03.380
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Well, the deed of absolute sale, counsel, if at all, the deed of absolute sale would be the final document that you execute in order to transfer the property. Ngayon, kung bahagi pa siya ng mother title, hindi ka naman mag-i-issue ng title, diba? I don't know if you've tried buying from a subdivision. Hindi ka naman mag-i-issue ng title. Carve it out from the mother title in an installment sale and then annotate at the back that it's for installment. You will issue the title simply after it has been fully paid. That's the common practice.

01:47:03.500 --> 01:47:43.720
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: But our point is, Your Honor, there is nowhere in the documents which would indicate that the property covered by this TCT was agreed to be paid in an installment basis or that a contract to sell was executed before a deed of absolute sale was executed 2018. And of course, your Honor, it is common sometimes a contract to sell is first executed if there are installment basis and then after all of the payments have been made, then they execute the deed of absolute sale. But that is not an absolute requirement. It is also completely possible that you go directly to a DOAS.

01:47:43.940 --> 01:47:50.000
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Now, my next question, Attorney Tolosa, is forgive me if I'm asking you these questions because it goes to the heart of the theory of the prosecution.

01:47:50.240 --> 01:47:50.640
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Yes, Your Honor.

01:47:52.420 --> 01:48:05.650
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: In both these parcels of land that you claim the Vice President did not declare, the one in Davao City and the one in... and IGACOS. You took issue at the fact na magkaiba yung acquisition cost.

01:48:05.850 --> 01:48:06.090
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: That's

01:48:06.090 --> 01:48:06.270
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: correct.

01:48:06.690 --> 01:48:21.210
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Siyempre, sasabihin ni Atty. Lindon, ang nilagay acquisition cost sa SALN, iba naman yung binayaran talaga, which will include transfer taxes, capital gains tax, doc stamps, whatever. Or, yung totoong presyo.

01:48:21.370 --> 01:48:21.970
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Yes, sir.

01:48:22.150 --> 01:49:04.940
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kasi di ba usually in deed of sale, binababahan yan? It's common practice. As long as it is in excess of the Assessed value, you usually put it below the market value, hindi naman illegal yun, para mas mababa, hindi ba? Yung capital gains tax, transfer taxes, doc stamps, at iba pa. So, is it your contention na if the Vice President declared this, she would have over-declared? Na ang value ng lupa based on the deed of sale is only 3 million but she declared 4 million? Na ang value ng lupa dun sa Davao City is how much? 4 million? Dineclare niya 10 million. Aside from the inconsistency, is it possible she over-declared?

01:49:06.100 --> 01:49:09.660
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: First of all, thank you for the question and the opportunity to explain this.

01:49:09.720 --> 01:49:10.060
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, please.

01:49:10.320 --> 01:49:43.920
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: With respect to the acquisition cost, Memorandum Circular No. 2, Series of 2013, issued by the Civil Service Commission with the subject revised statement of assets, liabilities, and net worth form. Page 4. Acquisition cost is the amount of money paid to acquire or own something. Now, if we correlate this with the Civil Code, Your Honor, in order for a transfer of ownership, in order for a sale to be consummated, in order for a person to own something, all you need to do is to fulfill the requirements for a valid contract. You just need to

01:49:43.920 --> 01:50:29.770
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: have a meeting of the minds, an object certain, and the consideration. All of these taxes In fees, they are not required to own something, to acquire something. You just need them possibly so that you'll be able to transfer the property under your name. In fact, under the same rules, you are required to declare in the SALN a real property that you bought. With a deed of absolute sale, even if that property has not yet been transferred under your name. So it is clear, if you will reconcile all of these provisions together, for the acquisition cost, you don't have to and you shouldn't include the taxes and the fees because you did not pay them to acquire it.

01:50:30.350 --> 01:51:00.620
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: But if I want to be safe, isn't it better to over-declare? What I paid instead of under-declaring it because I will be placed in this situation. Na yung dineklara ko, mababa dun sa aktual. Hindi ba para maging safe ka, iaakyat mo? Meaning, now my question is, is that a crime? Because right now, the crime is not to declare.

01:51:01.250 --> 01:51:01.930
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Yes, sir.

01:51:02.110 --> 01:51:25.330
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Now, is it your position that it's also a crime if at all to over... Declare? Meaning, tama ka. Basis sa guidelines, hindi mo kailangan na deklara. Eh gusto ko eh, para klaro. Ito naman talaga yung binayad ko eh. Ngayon, minaji ko ng konti yung deed of sale eh, para mas mababay. Di ba, as a lawyer, you know that. Lawyers and accountants do that. Advise that to

01:51:25.330 --> 01:51:25.770
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: their clients.

01:51:25.870 --> 01:51:27.130
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: I don't, Your Honor, for the record.

01:51:27.270 --> 01:51:27.670
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Within the

01:51:27.670 --> 01:51:43.270
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: bounds of law, of course, because it's not technically illegal. As long as, di ba, pasok ka. Now, gusto niya i-declare yung totoong binayad. Now, is that a violation of the SALN law? Is there a provision that says it's a violation? Admittedly, you don't have to.

01:51:43.530 --> 01:51:43.990
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: But

01:51:43.990 --> 01:51:46.010
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: if you do, did you violate anything?

01:51:46.670 --> 01:51:50.450
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: First and foremost, Your Honor, our position is these are not the same properties.

01:51:50.650 --> 01:51:51.030
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: And

01:51:51.030 --> 01:51:57.330
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: the proposition that she just over-declared it, first of all,

01:51:59.310 --> 01:52:24.810
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: We will not take that position because there are clear guidelines that must be followed in filling up your SALN form. And as I've explained, based on these guidelines, you don't need to put those figures because they're not part of the acquisition cost. Now, if they will take the position that she did, Your Honor, that is speculation. The only person who could say that is the Vice President and she will have to take the stand and make that explanation, Your Honor.

01:52:24.950 --> 01:52:28.210
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I'm going there. Attorney Lindon, is that the...

01:52:29.800 --> 01:52:32.460
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: If you are claiming that this is the same property,

01:52:32.720 --> 01:52:34.660
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: given

01:52:34.660 --> 01:52:58.120
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: that the respective deeds of sale submitted by you yourself and by the witness you presented yesterday and today indicated lower amounts in the deed of sale compared to the declared acquisition cost, is it your position that aside from

01:52:59.850 --> 01:53:22.890
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: In-include yung mga transfer, capital gains, kung anumang taxes, transfer taxes, doc stamps sa pag-transfer. If it's your position that it's the same property, then the Vice President over-declared. Did not under-declare but over-declared. Would that be a correct statement of your position?

01:53:23.710 --> 01:53:42.130
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Your Honor, the position of the defense as early as when this allegation came up is that the acquisition cost includes not just the purchase price but also all the other taxes or expenses relative to that transaction.

01:53:42.150 --> 01:53:52.130
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I computed it, Attorney Lindon. It's still more than that. You're talking roughly, capital gains tax, kahit siya pa sumagot, transfer taxes, doc stamps.

01:53:53.690 --> 01:53:59.600
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: It won't reach 12% of total.

01:54:01.420 --> 01:54:13.920
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Please correct me if I'm wrong. So, malaki pa rin yung dineclare ng Vice President eh, kumpara dun sa sale price plus the transfer taxes.

01:54:15.780 --> 01:54:19.200
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: It will still not match. I doubt if it will match.

01:54:19.620 --> 01:54:24.540
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Yes, Your Honor. But our position remains that this is the...

01:54:26.120 --> 01:54:48.000
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: These are the same property which are declared in the Statement of Assets, Liabilities, and Net Worth. And that there are other expenses which make up the cost of acquisition declared in the SALN, Your Honor. Aside from the taxes and other expenses, Your Honor.

01:54:48.240 --> 01:54:48.820
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Or baka

01:54:48.820 --> 01:54:50.440
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: posibleng yun ang totoong binayaran niya?

01:54:51.140 --> 01:54:52.000
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Yes, Your Honor.

01:54:52.300 --> 01:54:52.820
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Meaning,

01:54:52.960 --> 01:54:54.000
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: between

01:54:54.000 --> 01:55:11.120
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: the parties, di ba? So, hindi man tumugma yung dinagdag nating transfer taxes, capital gains tax, doc stamps, at iba pa, baka diniklara lamang niya yung totoong ginastos sa binayari niya. Is that the supposition of the respondent?

01:55:11.560 --> 01:55:14.820
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: We don't want to speculate in that regard, Your Honor.

01:55:15.160 --> 01:55:15.600
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Okay.

01:55:15.720 --> 01:55:16.160
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank

01:55:16.160 --> 01:55:16.640
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: you very much.

01:55:17.100 --> 01:55:20.000
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Your Honor, last word, then the matter, please. If I'd be allowed to just...

01:55:21.350 --> 01:55:30.350
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: With your permission, Attorney Tolosa, I will not allow it because it's not a debate between you and him, Attorney Lindon. Yes, Senator Judge Villanueva.

01:55:30.670 --> 01:55:32.430
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Yes, thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

01:55:32.510 --> 01:55:34.750
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Unless Senator Judge Joel will...

01:55:34.750 --> 01:55:40.690
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Yeah, I will, I will, Your Honor. Not because we come from the same university.

01:55:42.250 --> 01:56:22.540
Sen. Joel Villanueva: No, just to put on record, kasi kanina, it's very clear sa akin yung answer ng witness na The same property with the tax declaration and the description of the property. And now you're saying, attorney, from the prosecution that these are not the same property. So, what would be the strongest evidence at strongest position to convince us These are two different properties, Your Honor.

01:56:22.620 --> 01:57:47.340
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Thank you for that, Perchutio. The statement, the admission of the witness himself, which we again, we have to take the witness's candor in answering our statements. Our witness stated that the property covered by the subject TCT is not the same as that one declared in the SALN. They presented witness to disprove that fact. And this witness clearly admitted that he cannot say With absolute certainty, he is not certain that that property disclosed in the SALN is the same property declared in the TCT. The witness confirmed this twice. So since this is their witness that they presented to disprove our allegation, clearly, they were not able to disprove it. And aside from his admissions, Your Honor, again, the glaring discrepancies, Your Honor, of the... For example, as we've mentioned already, the purchase price versus the acquisition cost. It's clear, again, I've already stated the provisions in the guidelines governing the filing of SALNs, which states you should not include in the acquisition cost the taxes and the transfer fees. And it's clear that these statements from the defense that they could have been included is nothing more than Speculation. There is no evidence that proves this at this point.

01:57:47.700 --> 01:57:48.220
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Again,

01:57:48.300 --> 01:58:32.980
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: as we've stated, it's only the Vice President who could state when she filled up the SALN and swore to it that when she indicated that amount, she included those transfer fees. Second, Your Honor, the date of acquisition, there's a glaring discrepancy. 2019 versus, sorry, 2013 versus 2018. So, clearly, These are completely different properties. And as aptly pointed out by the presiding officer himself, even if you will include this piece, the amount will still not match the acquisition cost stated, which only leads to one logical conclusion. These are different properties, Your Honor.

01:58:33.200 --> 01:58:33.540
Sen. Joel Villanueva: At

01:58:33.540 --> 01:58:46.220
Sen. Joel Villanueva: kung ito ay magkaibang property, meron na po ba kayong naiisip or sa inyong pananaw? Nasaan itong isang property na ito? Exactly kung nasaan ito?

01:58:47.000 --> 01:59:07.120
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: It is for the Vice President to know where this property is indicated. But what we're certain is that this property indicated in the TCT, she did not declare it. Which is a clear violation of the law of the Constitution which is an impeachable offense.

01:59:08.860 --> 01:59:13.300
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Salamat po. Let's hear also from the defense.

01:59:14.000 --> 01:59:16.400
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Briefly, Atty. Lindon, we can pause for lunch.

