Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Counsel, I think he knows. Attorney Sheila,

01:59:52.060 --> 01:59:56.240
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: kindly, kindly, kindly let Attorney Tolosa finish and then we will recognize you.

01:59:57.280 --> 02:00:14.740
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Thank you, Your Honor. So again, as I've stated, I'm not objecting if they're asking for an exemption from the rules. All that we're saying, if this will be allowed moving forward, of course, we should be also allowed and given the same concession. That's all.

02:00:14.740 --> 02:00:15.060
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: Thank

02:00:15.060 --> 02:01:05.070
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: you, Your Honor. Well, it doesn't seem that the council is not objecting the fact that he took the microphone and said something about my taking the podium at this point is by itself an objection. But nonetheless, we'll proceed to also address the good Senator Villanueva's query and also in response to the lengthy quantification. To borrow his words of counsel for the prosecution. Now, they're saying that it's the respondent's burden to prove that these real property declared in her SALN is not... The same property registered with the city.

02:01:05.070 --> 02:01:06.690
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: That is not what we stated, Your Honor.

02:01:06.750 --> 02:01:06.790
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: Et cetera,

02:01:06.790 --> 02:01:08.670
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: et cetera. Well, to that effect.

02:01:08.790 --> 02:01:10.870
